 ## Overview
-EWA Splatting is a high-quality volume rendering technique that eliminates aliasing artifacts by replacing the standard footprint function with a band-limited resampling filter [S1, unofficial][S2][S8, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visual artifacts caused by incorrect visibility determination and sampling rate changes in perspective projections, which occur when reconstruction kernels overlap or when the sampling rate falls below the Nyquist frequency [S1, unofficial][S8, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from basic splatting by combining an elliptical Gaussian reconstruction kernel with a Gaussian low-pass filter to avoid aliasing, and from other variants by using a rigorous affine approximation of the projective mapping to derive an analytic 2D footprint [S2][S8, unofficial].
+EWA Splatting is a high-quality volume rendering technique that eliminates aliasing artifacts by replacing standard footprint functions with a band-limited resampling filter [S1, unofficial][S2][S9, S16, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visual holes and high-frequency noise inherent in basic splatting by combining an elliptical Gaussian reconstruction kernel with a Gaussian low-pass filter [S2][S5, S6, unofficial]. Unlike its siblings [Splatting Without the Blur](1157-splatting-without-the-blur.md) and [Splat Radius Adjustment Based on Normal Angle](1264-splat-radius-adjustment-based-on-normal-angle.md), which focus on geometric extent or radius heuristics, EWA Splatting derives an analytic, perspective-correct 2D footprint via local affine approximation of the projective transformation [S9, S16, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** Volume data represented as a set of particles (voxels), each with position $\mathbf{p}_k$, density/extinction coefficient $g_k$, color $c_{\lambda k}$, and a 3D elliptical Gaussian reconstruction kernel defined by variance matrix $\mathbf{V}_k$ in object space [S6, unofficial][S11]. Camera parameters: viewing transformation matrix $\mathbf{W}$ (rotational part mapping object to camera space) and projection matrix [S6, unofficial][S11].
-**Outputs:** Final 2D image with intensity $I_\lambda(\hat{\mathbf{x}})$ [S8, unofficial].
+**Inputs and Outputs:**
+*   **Input:** Volume data represented as a set of particles (voxels or samples), each with a position, a 3x3 variance matrix $\mathbf{V}_k$ defining the elliptical Gaussian reconstruction kernel, and optical properties (extinction $g_k$, emission $c_{\lambda k}$) [S6, S9, unofficial].
+*   **Output:** A 2D image where each pixel value is the accumulated color and opacity from overlapping splats [S6, S9, unofficial].
 
