 **Parameters:**
-*   $r$: Cutoff radius for the Gaussian kernel. Typical value: $1 \leq r \leq 3$ [S6, unofficial][S11].
-*   $\mathbf{V}_h$: Variance matrix of the low-pass filter. Usually $\mathbf{I}$ (identity) [S6, unofficial][S11].
-*   $\mathbf{W}$: Rotational part of the viewing transformation [S6, unofficial][S11].
+*   **Cutoff radius $r$:** Truncation limit for the Gaussian kernel. Typically $1 \le r \le 3$ [S6, unofficial][S12].
+*   **Low-pass filter $\mathbf{V}_h$:** Usually the 2x2 identity matrix [S6, unofficial][S12].
+*   **Shininess:** Used in shading passes, default 8.0 [S13, unofficial].
 
 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Division by Zero:** If a voxel is at the center of projection ($\mathbf{u}_k = 0$), the Jacobian is undefined. Skip such voxels or clamp depth [G].
-*   **Numerical Stability:** The condition number of the inverse 2D-to-2D projective mapping increases rapidly when the projection approaches a line, causing numerical instability in centralized conics approaches [S12, unofficial].
-*   **Underestimation:** Approximations of screen-space extents can underestimate splat sizes, causing splats to be chopped off. A safety factor $> 1$ fixes this but generates unnecessary fragments [S12, unofficial].
-*   **Non-Symmetric Kernels:** If 3D reconstruction kernels are not radially symmetric (e.g., sheared, anisotropic), additional care is required to ensure contributions sum correctly [S9, unofficial].
+*   **Singularity:** If $u_{k_2} \to 0$ (point at center of projection), the Jacobian becomes singular. The point should be clipped or handled separately [S6, unofficial].
+*   **Non-overlapping Assumption:** Basic splatting assumes non-overlapping kernels, which causes aliasing. EWA handles overlap via the resampling filter, but compositing order (back-to-front) remains critical for correct transparency [S1, S9, unofficial].
+*   **Numerical Stability:** The inverse of the 2x2 matrix $\mathbf{M}_k$ can be unstable if the ellipse is degenerate (e.g., viewed edge-on). A safety factor or regularization may be needed [S13, unofficial].
+*   **Notation:** A hat symbol ($\hat{\mathbf{V}}$) denotes skipping the third row and column [S6, unofficial][S12].
 
